2026-10-22|Minimum Adjacent ASCII Difference for a Palindrome

Question:
Given a string s consisting of lowercase English letters and '?':

- Replace every '?' with a lowercase English letter so that s becomes a palindrome.
- Minimize the sum of absolute ASCII differences between every pair of adjacent characters.
- Return the minimum sum, or -1 if forming a palindrome is impossible.

Approach:
1. Use two pointers, one at the beginning and one at the end of the string.
2. Compare the characters at the mirrored positions.
   - If both are letters and different, forming a palindrome is impossible, so return -1.
   - If both are letters and equal, keep them unchanged.
   - If one is '?' and the other is a letter, replace '?' with that letter.
   - If both are '?', temporarily leave them unresolved.
3. After resolving mirrored pairs, assign a letter to each unresolved pair. To minimize adjacent differences, consider the neighboring fixed characters. A simple optimal choice for a run of unresolved positions is to use the same letter throughout, chosen to minimize the differences at the run's boundaries.
4. Calculate the sum of absolute ASCII differences between each pair of adjacent characters.
5. Return the total.

Solution:
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

class Solution {
public:
    long long minimumCost(string s) {
        int n = s.size();

        // Enforce palindrome constraints.
        for (int i = 0; i < n / 2; i++) {
            int j = n - 1 - i;

            if (s[i] != '?' && s[j] != '?' && s[i] != s[j]) {
                return -1;
            }

            if (s[i] == '?' && s[j] != '?') {
                s[i] = s[j];
            } else if (s[j] == '?' && s[i] != '?') {
                s[j] = s[i];
            }
        }

        // A palindrome has mirrored characters equal.
        // Fill each unresolved mirrored pair with the same letter.
        for (int i = 0; i < n / 2; i++) {
            int j = n - 1 - i;

            if (s[i] == '?' && s[j] == '?') {
                char chosen = 'a';

                // Prefer a neighboring fixed character when available.
                if (i > 0 && s[i - 1] != '?') {
                    chosen = s[i - 1];
                } else if (j + 1 < n && s[j + 1] != '?') {
                    chosen = s[j + 1];
                }

                s[i] = s[j] = chosen;
            }
        }

        if (n % 2 == 1 && s[n / 2] == '?') {
            s[n / 2] = (n / 2 > 0) ? s[n / 2 - 1] : 'a';
        }

        // Compute adjacent ASCII differences.
        long long answer = 0;

        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            answer += abs((int)s[i] - (int)s[i - 1]);
        }

        return answer;
    }
};

Time Complexity: O(n), because the string is traversed a constant number of times.

Space Complexity: O(1) auxiliary space, excluding the string storage.
